.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH YR-EXTRACT 1 "" YARA-X "User Commands"
.SH NAME
yr\-extract \- Extract data from container files
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fByr extract\fR [\fB\-\-max\-depth\fR] [\fB\-\-vba\-max\-extracted\-files\fR] [\fB\-\-zip\-max\-extracted\-files\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE\fR> <\fIOUTPUT_DIR\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Extract data from a container file
.PP
Given a container file (e.g., a ZIP archive), this command unpacks its contents
recursively and saves the extracted files into the specified output directory,
printing the path of each extracted file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-depth\fR \fI<DEPTH>\fR [default: 3]
Maximum container extraction depth
.TP
\fB\-\-vba\-max\-extracted\-files\fR \fI<FILES>\fR [default: 1000]
Maximum number of files extracted per VBA document
.TP
\fB\-\-zip\-max\-extracted\-files\fR \fI<FILES>\fR [default: 1000]
Maximum number of files extracted per ZIP archive
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
Path to container file
.TP
<\fIOUTPUT_DIR\fR>
Output directory where extracted files will be saved
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fByr\fR(1)
